  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nEnsemble guidance remains in strong agreement that persistent\nupper ridging and surface high pressure will dominate the region\nthrough most of next week (if not longer). This will guarantee\ndry, sunny, and warm conditions. Precipitation chances remain\nbelow 10% through Thursday morning before cloud cover gradually\nincreases ahead of an approaching trough.\n\nUncertainty in ridge placement and trough movement grows by late\nnext week with increasing rain chances into the weekend. \nHowever, 24-hour probabilities generally never exceed 50% \nduring this timeframe, suggesting rain likely confined to one \nperiod (rather than multiple rounds) with models uncertain which\nof Friday/Saturday/Sunday sees the best chance.",
